※ pl4g-test: compile=error diag=4546

※ A unit is not a value: there is nothing at all for one to be while the
※ program runs, a unit being the part of a type the code knows nothing about.
※ So it is lifted out of the program the same way a type is where the compiler
※ is asked about one, and `⌜meter⌝` is what `⎕unit` is given.

@[startup]
fn main() → u6:
    let n: u32 = 5u32
    let m: u32 ¤meter = ⎕unit(n, 3u32)
    0u6
